<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ulan Butung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1690">1690</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungar-qing-wars">Dzungar–Qing Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ulan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buton-island">Butung</a> was fought in September 1690 a few hundred kilometres north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galdan-boshugtu-khan">Galdan Boshugtu Khan</a> and a Qing army led by Prince Fuquan, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangxi-emperor">Kangxi Emperor</a>'s half-brother. Galdan's troops fought behind a line of kneeling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a> covered with felt, and the battle was indecisive, but Galdan withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> with heavy losses. The Qing went on to defeat him at Jao Modo in 1696.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ulan-butung.jpg" alt="Battle of Ulan Butung" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 范承烈 (Fan Chenglie) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qing_artillery_and_musketeers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
